<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Finding the mistake in a locus from a line</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Kiprono was asked for the locus of points \({@d@}\) units from the line \({@vs@} = {@c@}\). He wrote: [[if test="is(er=1)"]]the line \({@vs@} = {@c+d@}\)[[elif test="is(er=2)"]]the lines \({@vs@} = {@exd(c-d/2)@}\) and \({@vs@} = {@exd(c+d/2)@}\)[[else]]the lines \({@vs@} = {@d@}\) and \({@vs@} = {@-d@}\)[[/if]].</p><p>(a) What is wrong with his answer?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Give the correct locus.</p><div>The lines \({@vs@} = \) [[input:ans2]] and \({@vs@} = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Give the locus of points equidistant from the lines \({@vs@} = {@c@}\) and \({@vs@} = {@c2@}\).</p><div>\({@vs@} = \) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) [[if test="is(er=1)"]]The points \({@d@}\) units from a line lie on both sides of it: Kiprono has given only one of the two lines.[[elif test="is(er=2)"]]Each of his lines is only \({@exd(d/2)@}\) units from \({@vs@} = {@c@}\): he has used half the distance on each side.[[else]]His lines are \({@d@}\) units from the axis \({@vs@} = 0\), not from \({@vs@} = {@c@}\).[[/if]]</p><p>(b) The locus is a pair of lines parallel to \({@vs@} = {@c@}\), one on each side and each \({@d@}\) units from it: \({@vs@} = {@c@} - {@d@} = {@c-d@}\) and \({@vs@} = {@c@} + {@d@} = {@c+d@}\).</p><p>(c) Points equidistant from two parallel lines lie on the parallel line halfway between them: \({@vs@} = \dfrac{ {#msum#} }{2} = {@mid@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
/* Design: find the mistake in a locus at a distance from a line. o 0: horizontal lines (y = c); 1: vertical (x = c). er 1: one line only; 2: half the distance; 3: distance from the axis. Source: original. */
o: rand(2);
vs: ["y","x"][o+1];
c: rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]);
d: rand_with_prohib(2,6,[abs(c)]);
er: 1+rand(3);
kk: rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[-1,0,1,c]);
c2: c+2*kk;
mid: c+kk;
/* the midline sum shows a negative second line in brackets, not "1 + -9" */
msum: if is(c2<0) then sconcat(c, " + (", c2, ")") else sconcat(c, " + ", c2);
o1: [["ok",false,"Nothing: Kiprono is right"],["one",is(er=1),"He has given only one of the two lines"],["half",is(er=2),"He has used half the distance on each side"],["axis",is(er=3),"He has measured the distance from the axis, not from the line"]];
ta1: ["one","half","axis"][er];
wk1: first(sublist(["one","half","axis"], lambda([z], is(z#ta1))));
/* (b) diagnostics as sorted pairs: half the distance; Kiprono's lines (er 1) or the lines measured from the axis (er 2, 3) */
hf: [c-d/2, c+d/2];
hl: if is(er=1) then [c+d, c+d] else [-d, d];]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
